.TH VAC-REGISTER 8 "2026-05-30" "versatile-autoreg-vac" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vac-register \- Point-in-time registration and extra-field management for VAC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vac-register
.RB [ \-\-imperative | \-\-informative ]
.B \-\-key
.I KEY
.RB { source | \-d }
.br
.B vac-register
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vac-register
performs a one-shot self-check and registration against the VAS server
configured in
.IR /etc/vac/vac.conf .
If the current hostname, IP, MAC and extra fields match
.IR /var/lib/vac/identity.json ,
no request is sent.
.PP
It is also used to insert, update, or delete individual keys in the
persistent extra-field state without waiting for the next
.BR vac (8)
cycle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-imperative
Operate on the
.B extra_imperative
dictionary. Changes to this dictionary bump the VAS inventory version.
.TP
.B \-\-informative
Operate on the
.B extra_informative
dictionary. Changes never bump the version.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " KEY"
The extra-field key to insert, update, or delete.
.TP
.I source
Path to a file containing the JSON value for
.IR KEY ,
or
.B \-
to read from standard input.
.TP
.B \-d
Delete
.I KEY
from the selected dictionary.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Operate on sub-instance
.I NAME
instead of the main instance.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set a key in the imperative dictionary from a file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vac-register \-\-imperative \-\-key cups /tmp/cups.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Delete a key from the informative dictionary:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vac-register \-\-informative \-\-key hardware \-d
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vac/vac.conf
Configuration file shared with
.BR vac (8).
.TP
.I /var/lib/vac/extras_imperative.json
.TQ
.I /var/lib/vac/extras_informative.json
Persistent extra-field state with per-key timestamps.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vac (8),
.BR vac-sub-instance (8)
